Subject: [PATCH] ucode: reject interrupted handler initialization

ucode now reports STATUS_BREAK when execution is suspended by a break
request. Handler initialization must complete before its callback can be
used; uhttpd has no debugger resume loop here. Report an interrupted
initialization as an error, as for other non-completing executions.

This also keeps the exhaustive status switch building with the newer
ucode headers and -Werror=switch.

--- a/ucode.c
+++ b/ucode.c
@@ -305,6 +305,10 @@
 		fprintf(stderr, "Error: Compilation error while executing ucode handler\n");
 		exit(1);
 
+	case STATUS_BREAK:
+		fprintf(stderr, "Error: Execution interrupted while initializing ucode handler\n");
+		exit(2);
+
 	case ERROR_RUNTIME:
 		fprintf(stderr, "Error: Runtime error while executing ucode handler\n");
 		exit(2);
